 "result_text": "I fixed the bug in `rachiopy/rachioobject.py`. I haven't run it against the Rachio API or the tests.\n\nThe cause was in `_request`. It passed the dict payload straight to `requests` as `data=`, so the body went out form-encoded instead of as JSON. The server then failed to parse it, giving the \"Unrecognized token 'device'\" error.\n\n`_request` now serializes the body with `json.dumps` before sending it. Strings and bytes pass through unchanged. This is in the shared helper, so every call that sends a body now gets JSON. That covers `notification.add` and `notification.update`, and also the device, zone and schedule rule `put_request` calls, which were sending form data too. I didn't change any tests.",
